{"id":"0080e2f9f7e26ee536dcfa217d71edf644467d3f","axis":"silent","repo":"symfony/symfony","sha":"0080e2f9f7e26ee536dcfa217d71edf644467d3f","parsed":{"files":[{"path":"UPGRADE-8.2.md","lines":["@@ -213,6 +213,7 @@ HttpClient","  * [BC BREAK] An explicit `http_version` of `2.0` makes `CurlHttpClient` and `AmpHttpClient` require HTTP/2: they use prior knowledge on `http://` URLs instead of offering an upgrade, and offer only `h2` during the TLS handshake on `https://` URLs (with curl 8.10 or higher); servers that speak only HTTP/1.1 are not reachable that way anymore, unset the option for them","  * [BC BREAK] Redirects from `https://` to `http://` URLs are not followed anymore. The 3xx response is returned instead, and its `redirect_url` info contains the target URL. Request that URL yourself if you want to follow the redirect","  * `KernelTestCase::ensureKernelShutdown()` now clears the responses cached in the `cache.http_client` pool when `framework.test` is enabled, so that each test starts with no cached response. A test that relied on a response cached by a previous test, or before a kernel shutdown in the same test, should request it itself","+ * Add argument `$shutdown` to `reset()` in `DecoratorTrait`, `ScopingHttpClient` and `ThrottlingHttpClient`"," "," HttpFoundation"," --------------"],"additions":1,"deletions":0,"truncated":false},{"path":"phpstan.dist.neon","lines":["@@ -72,9 +72,7 @@ parameters:","         # reset() keeps its optional argument virtual for subclasses","         -","             message: '#^PHPDoc tag @param references unknown parameter\\: \\$shutdown$#'","-            paths:","-                - src/Symfony/Component/DependencyInjection/Container.php","-                - src/Symfony/Bundle/FrameworkBundle/Test/TestContainer.php","+            path: src/Symfony/*","         # The deprecated HttpKernel wrapper keeps its parent class for BC.","         -","             identifier: class.extendsFinalByPhpDoc"],"additions":1,"deletions":3,"tr